@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Analysis invariant to physical enforcement and evidence
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Authoritative analysis / dictionary\nMeaning, ownership, lifecycle and source status" as A
rectangle "Logical record families\nIdentity, scope, revisions and relationships" as L
rectangle "Row / relationship constraints\nPK, FK, unique, requiredness, evaluated checks" as R
rectangle "Guarded local transactions\nVersions, locks, cross-record invariants" as T
rectangle "Storage / external coordination\nProtected references, durable intent, reconciliation" as E
rectangle "Physical mapping specification\nExact engine/types/collation/indexes/DDL still gated" as P
rectangle "Verification evidence\nActual constraint, concurrency, query and restore checks" as V
A --> L : refine without accepting proposed counts
L --> R : allocate structural invariants
L --> T : allocate concurrent local invariants
L --> E : allocate cross-store / remote invariants
R --> P
T --> P
E --> P
P --> V : evaluate the real candidate
note bottom of V
 A foreign key is not authorization.
 SQL rollback is not remote rollback.
 Schema existence is not recoverability evidence.
end note
@enduml
